[0.050, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.039, "o", "\r\n  DEMO  lerobot/svla_so101_pickplace\r\n        the official SO-101 example, 50 episodes, metadata only, bundled with this package (Apache-2.0).\r\n        Run `orbit status` in a folder with your own dataset to see yours.\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n  WHERE YOU ARE\r\n    recorded: 50 episodes, 398 seconds, so100_follower\r\n    joints:   6 (shoulder_pan.pos, shoulder_lift.pos, elbow_flex.pos, ...)\r\n    trained:  nothing yet\r\n    evaluated: no trials logged\r\n\r\n  WHAT'S WRONG\r\n    the command to elbow_flex.pos was clipped at the end of its range\r\n      commanded +100, the limit of the normalised range\r\n    the command to shoulder_lift.pos was clipped at the end of its range\r\n      commanded -100, the limit of the normalised range\r\n\r\n  NEXT ACTION\r\n    fix elbow_flex.pos first: the command was clipped at the end of its\r\n    range. Re-record those episodes before you read anything into a success\r\n    rate. 1 other like it.\r\n\r\n  WHAT A BATTERY BUYS\r\n      10 trials  ->  resolves a drop of  44.7 points  <- the guide's default\r\n      20 trials  ->  resolves a drop of  31.6 points\r\n      50 trials  ->  resolves a drop of  20.0 points\r\n     100 trials  ->  resolves a drop of  14.1 points\r\n     200 trials  ->  resolves a drop of  10.0 points\r\n\r\n    a trial is about"]
[0.000, "o", " a minute of standing at the robot, so the row you pick\r\n    is a time budget, not a statistical preference.\r\n\r\n  ALSO WORTH KNOWING\r\n    orbit cover  which instruction and workspace combinations were never recorded\r\n    orbit check  did the new policy break any job, with the interval\r\n    orbit next   retrain, collect demonstrations, or run more trials, per job\r\n    orbit log    one keypress per trial, standing at the robot\r\n\r\n"]
